#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:4
msgid "Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:6
msgid ""
"MLX uses environment variables to configure compilation, numerical "
"precision, backend behavior, and distributed execution. Set them before "
"starting the process. Many variables are read when the corresponding "
"subsystem is first initialized and changing them later may have no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:11
msgid ""
"Boolean variables use ``0`` to disable and a nonzero integer to enable "
"unless otherwise noted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:15
msgid "General"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:19
msgid ""
"Disable compilation globally. This variable is enabled by its presence, so "
"setting it to ``0`` also disables compilation. Calling :func:`mlx.core."
"enable_compile` overrides it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:25
msgid ""
"Allow reduced-precision ``float32`` matrix-multiplication family operations "
"on supported hardware. The default is ``1``. Set it to ``0`` to keep these "
"operations in full ``float32`` precision. See :doc:`precision`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:30
msgid "Distributed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:32
msgid ""
"The variables required to initialize a distributed process depend on the "
"backend. :doc:`distributed` describes their formats and how ``mlx.launch`` "
"sets them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:38
msgid ""
"The zero-based rank of the current process. This is used by the Ring, JACCL, "
"and NCCL backends. ``JACCL_RANK`` is accepted as a higher-priority alias by "
"JACCL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:44
msgid "The path to the JSON host file used by the Ring backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:48
msgid ""
"Enable verbose logging for the Ring backend. This variable is enabled by its "
"presence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:53
msgid ""
"The path to the JSON device-connectivity file used by JACCL. "
"``JACCL_IBV_DEVICES`` is accepted as a higher-priority alias."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:58
msgid ""
"The coordinator address in ``IP:port`` form used to establish JACCL "
"connections. ``JACCL_COORDINATOR`` is accepted as a higher-priority alias."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:63
msgid ""
"Prefer a ring topology for JACCL. This variable is enabled by its presence. "
"``JACCL_RING`` is accepted as a higher-priority alias."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:68
msgid "The total number of processes in an NCCL group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:72
msgid ""
"The timeout in milliseconds for establishing NCCL bootstrap connections. The "
"default is ``300000``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:77
msgid ""
"Override the MPI dynamic-library name. The default is ``libmpi.dylib`` on "
"macOS and ``libmpi.so`` on other platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:80
msgid ""
"The NCCL backend also requires ``NCCL_HOST_IP`` and ``NCCL_PORT``. Setting "
"``NCCL_DEBUG=INFO`` enables additional logging while MLX establishes the "
"bootstrap connection. NCCL itself recognizes additional `NCCL environment "
"variables <https://docs.nvidia.com/deeplearning/nccl/user-guide/docs/env."
"html>`_. ``CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` selects the local CUDA device for each "
"process and is handled by the CUDA runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:88
msgid "Metal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:92
msgid ""
"Enable the faster Metal CPU/GPU synchronization path. The default is ``0``. "
"This requires Metal 3.2 or later (macOS 15 or later, or iOS 18 or later)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:96
msgid "Advanced tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:98
msgid ""
"These variables tune MLX implementation details. They are primarily intended "
"for development, diagnostics, and performance experiments. The defaults are "
"selected automatically for the current hardware and are appropriate for most "
"users. Their behavior may change as the implementation evolves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:105
msgid ""
"Set the breadth-first-search width limit used when constructing an "
"evaluation tape. The default is ``20``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:110
msgid ""
"Override the maximum number of operations encoded in one Metal command "
"buffer or CUDA graph. The default depends on the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:115
msgid ""
"Override the approximate memory limit, in megabytes, for one Metal command "
"buffer or CUDA graph. The default depends on the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:120
msgid ""
"Override the Metal GPU architecture string reported to MLX. This affects "
"architecture-specific kernel and scheduling choices, but does not change the "
"capabilities of the physical GPU. Forcing an architecture that does not "
"match the GPU can select incompatible kernels and produce incorrect results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:127
msgid ""
"Override the number of reduction blocks used by the Metal scaled dot-product "
"attention kernel. Positive values are rounded up to a multiple of ``32``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:132
msgid "CUDA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:134
msgid ""
"The MLX-prefixed variables in this section are advanced CUDA backend "
"controls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:138
msgid "Enable CUDA graph capture and replay. The default is ``1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:142
msgid ""
"Use the specified value as the filename prefix when writing captured CUDA "
"graphs to numbered DOT files. An unset or empty value disables the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:147
msgid ""
"Override the directory used to cache runtime-compiled PTX. By default MLX "
"uses an ``mlx/<version>/ptx`` directory under the system temporary directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:153
msgid ""
"Allow the CUDA backend to use cuDNN scaled dot-product attention when the "
"inputs and device are supported. The default is ``1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:158
msgid "Set the CUDA convolution cache capacity. The default is ``128``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:162
msgid "Set the CUDA FFT plan cache capacity. The default is ``128``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:166
msgid "Set the CUDA graph cache capacity. The default is ``400``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:170
msgid ""
"Set the CUDA forward scaled dot-product attention cache capacity. The "
"default is ``256``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:175
msgid ""
"Set the CUDA backward scaled dot-product attention cache capacity. The "
"default is ``64``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:180
msgid ""
"Detect repeated CUDA cache misses and raise an error suggesting a larger "
"cache capacity. The default is ``1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/usage/environment_variables.rst:183
msgid ""
"MLX also uses ``CUDA_HOME`` or ``CUDA_PATH`` to locate CUDA headers for "
"runtime kernel compilation when they cannot be found in the Python "
"environment."
msgstr ""
